option.RAY_TRACING=§4Ray Tracing
option.RAY_TRACING.comment=Ray traced light, cleaned up by a temporal and a spatial denoiser. Off gives vanilla lighting, which is the fastest.
option.RT_COLOR_TRACING=§cAdvanced Color Tracing
option.RT_COLOR_TRACING.comment=Every light source shines in the colour of its own texture, like a deep blue around soul torches, and stained glass colours the light that passes through it.
option.RT_BOUNCES=Light Bounces
option.RT_BOUNCES.comment=How many times light can bounce. Weak paths end early, so many bounces cost less than it sounds. Each extra bounce brightens enclosed rooms a little more.
option.RT_DISTANCE=Ray Distance
option.RT_DISTANCE.comment=How far a bounce ray can travel. Only what is on screen can be hit. Long rays need more steps to find thin objects.
value.RT_DISTANCE.16=1 chunk
value.RT_DISTANCE.32=2 chunks
value.RT_DISTANCE.64=4 chunks
value.RT_DISTANCE.128=8 chunks
value.RT_DISTANCE.256=16 chunks
option.RT_STEPS=Ray Steps
option.RT_STEPS.comment=How carefully each bounce ray searches. More steps find thin objects better, and cost more.
option.DENOISER_RADIUS=Denoiser Width
option.DENOISER_RADIUS.comment=How wide the two denoiser passes reach. Wider is smoother, but softens the bounce light.
option.RT_BLOCK_LIGHT=§cRay Traced Block Light
option.RT_BLOCK_LIGHT.comment=Torches, glowstone and lava light their surroundings in their own colour and cast real shadows, also when they are off screen. Costs some speed, most of it in the shadow pass.
option.RT_LIGHT_FILL=Soft Fill Light
option.RT_LIGHT_FILL.comment=How much of the vanilla light level stays on top of the ray traced light. At 0%, the standard, shadows from block light are as dark as if the light were not there. Higher values brighten them.
value.RT_LIGHT_FILL.0=0%
value.RT_LIGHT_FILL.15=15%
value.RT_LIGHT_FILL.30=30%
value.RT_LIGHT_FILL.50=50%
value.RT_LIGHT_FILL.75=75%
value.RT_LIGHT_FILL.100=100%

screen.SMOKE_FOG=§6Smoke §7& §3Fog
option.VOLUMETRIC_SMOKE=§6Volumetric Smoke
option.VOLUMETRIC_SMOKE.comment=Torches, campfires, fire and lava give off rising, curling smoke that takes the glow of its source. It replaces the flat grey smoke particles above them.
option.VOLUMETRIC_FOG=§3Volumetric Fog
option.VOLUMETRIC_FOG.comment=Floating mist in deep caves, fog that rolls in with rain and storms, and thick glowing fog in the Nether.
option.CAVE_FOG_DENSITY=§7Cave Smoke Density
option.CAVE_FOG_DENSITY.comment=How thick the mist in deep caves is. It is lit by the torches and lava around it.
option.WEATHER_FOG_INTENSITY=§9Weather Fog Intensity
option.WEATHER_FOG_INTENSITY.comment=How thick the fog that comes with rain and thunderstorms is.
option.NETHER_FOG_DENSITY=§cNether Volumetric Density
option.NETHER_FOG_DENSITY.comment=How thick the fog in the Nether is. It takes the colour of the biome and glows orange above the lava sea.
suffix.CAVE_FOG_DENSITY=%
suffix.WEATHER_FOG_INTENSITY=%
suffix.NETHER_FOG_DENSITY=%

screen.WEATHER=§9Weather §7& §6Materials
option.RAIN_REFRACTION=§bRain Refraction
option.RAIN_REFRACTION.comment=Every raindrop is a small lens that bends the image behind it. Drops also catch the light of the sun, the moon and nearby torches.
option.RAIN_OPACITY=Rain Visibility
option.RAIN_OPACITY.comment=How clearly the falling rain shows.
option.WEATHER_SPLASH_QUALITY=§bRain Ripples
option.WEATHER_SPLASH_QUALITY.comment=Raindrops ring puddles, wet ground and water, and the rings show in the reflections. Higher quality adds more and finer rings.
value.WEATHER_SPLASH_QUALITY.0=§7Off
value.WEATHER_SPLASH_QUALITY.1=§aLow
value.WEATHER_SPLASH_QUALITY.2=§eMedium
value.WEATHER_SPLASH_QUALITY.3=§4High
option.SNOW_WIND_DRIFT=§fSnow Wind Drift
option.SNOW_WIND_DRIFT.comment=How strongly the wind blows the snow sideways and swirls it around.
suffix.RAIN_OPACITY=%
suffix.SNOW_WIND_DRIFT=%
option.SNOW_QUALITY=§fRain & Snow
option.SNOW_QUALITY.comment=Rain and snow in real depth, drawn by the pack: soft flakes and thin streaks that lean with the wind and catch the light of torches. They never fall under a roof. Ultra adds more layers further away.
value.SNOW_QUALITY.1=§e3D Smooth
value.SNOW_QUALITY.2=§4Ultra
option.GLASS_WEATHER_EFFECTS=§bWeather on Glass
option.GLASS_WEATHER_EFFECTS.comment=In rain, drops sit on windows and run slowly down them, bending the view through the glass. In snow, frost grows in from the edges of the panes.
option.GROUND_SPLASH_PARTICLES=§bRain Splashes
option.GROUND_SPLASH_PARTICLES.comment=Tiny droplets jump up where the rain hits the ground. Heavier rain throws more of them, and higher.
screen.CAMERA=§4Camera Effects
screen.DIMENSIONS=§4Dimensions
screen.PBR_PHYSICS=§4PBR & Physics
option.DEPTH_OF_FIELD=§4Depth of Field
option.DEPTH_OF_FIELD.comment=Blurs what is in front of and behind the point in the middle of the screen, like a camera lens. The focus follows smoothly as you look around.
option.DOF_STRENGTH=Blur Strength
suffix.DOF_STRENGTH=%
option.LENS_FLARE=§4Lens Flare
option.LENS_FLARE.comment=Ghosts of the aperture and a starburst when the sun or moon is in view. Clouds and terrain in front of it dim the flare.
option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH=Flare Strength
suffix.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH=%
option.LENS_DIRT=§4Lens Dirt
option.LENS_DIRT.comment=Smudges and dust on the lens, which only show where a bright light shines through them.
option.LENS_DIRT_STRENGTH=Dirt Strength
suffix.LENS_DIRT_STRENGTH=%
option.NETHER_HEAT_HAZE=§4Nether Heat Haze
option.NETHER_HEAT_HAZE.comment=Hot air shimmers high above the lava seas of the Nether.
option.NETHER_LIGHT_SHAFTS=§4Nether Light Shafts
option.NETHER_LIGHT_SHAFTS.comment=The fog of the Nether takes on the colour of the lights in it, and glowstone and fire cast shafts of light through it. Needs ray traced block light.
option.END_AURORA=§4Void Aurora
option.END_AURORA.comment=Curtains of blue and violet light wave slowly across the sky of the End.
option.END_AURORA_BRIGHTNESS=Aurora Brightness
suffix.END_AURORA_BRIGHTNESS=%
option.END_CRYSTAL_RAYS=§4End Crystal Rays
option.END_CRYSTAL_RAYS.comment=End crystals glow and send slowly turning rays of light out into the dark.
option.DYNAMIC_PUDDLES=§4Dynamic Puddles
option.DYNAMIC_PUDDLES.comment=Rain fills dips in the ground first and spreads to flat ground as it goes on. After the rain, puddles shrink again, faster in the sun. Nothing under a roof gets wet.
option.PUDDLE_AMOUNT=Puddle Amount
suffix.PUDDLE_AMOUNT=%
option.SSS_STRENGTH=Light Through Leaves
suffix.SSS_STRENGTH=%
option.TILT_SHIFT=§4Tilt-Shift / Miniature Mode
option.TILT_SHIFT.comment=A soft lens blur at the top and the bottom of the screen, with a sharp band across the middle, which makes the world look like a miniature model.
option.TILT_SHIFT_STRENGTH=Miniature Blur
suffix.TILT_SHIFT_STRENGTH=%
option.TILT_SHIFT_BAND=Sharp Band Height
suffix.TILT_SHIFT_BAND=%
option.VOLUMETRIC_CHECKERBOARD=§4Checkerboard Volumetrics
option.VOLUMETRIC_CHECKERBOARD.comment=Fog, god rays, clouds and smoke compute half of their pixels in each frame, and the temporal filter fills in the other half. Nearly the same image for about half the cost.
